From 3e42c47a8e38181fd5e743911efe4d0ef1c2e872 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 17:42:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 115/638] [AROS] Add tracked pre-MMU PartitionAlloc backing

AI_PHASE: chromium-phase-3
AI_STATUS: implementation
ROOT_CAUSE: KrnAllocPages delegates to the kernel mm_linear allocator, but transition-era Exec MemHeaders are not initialized through KrnInitMemory; hosted 0115 proved an unhinted 1 GiB request failed despite a 3 GiB largest free block.
FIX_REASON: Keep KrnAllocPages as the preferred backend and provide an unhinted, page-aligned AllocMem fallback with explicit backing records, retained alignment slack, exact final ownership release, and zero-before-recommit semantics.
SCOPE: base/allocator/partition_allocator/src/partition_alloc/page_allocator.cc; base/allocator/partition_allocator/src/partition_alloc/page_allocator_internals_aros.h
VALIDATION: AROS PartitionAlloc page_allocator.o cross-compiled; unattended 0115 diagnostics ruled out capacity and fragmentation at the kernel page boundary.
RISK: The fallback consumes physical Exec backing and retains alignment slack until final free; it is a bounded pre-MMU substrate, not sparse reservation, discard, or production W^X enforcement.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: 512 MiB pools -> unhinted 1 GiB allocation fails with 3 GiB contiguous -> mm_linear initialization gap -> tracked Exec backing bridge
Continues: d4b26ee0d8
